    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a mixed slate today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (63.25) and **Jacob Wilson** (62.77) as our premier options. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong dynamic platoon advantage against Woo, despite the respectable xERA, while **Jacob Wilson** earns his status as a core start based on favorable park factors that push his projected output well above his base level. **Nolan Schanuel** also grades out as a high-floor play (61.13) against Gage Jump; his ability to control the zone against a mid-rotation lefty makes him a reliable anchor in the lineup today, provided his projected #3 spot holds firm once official lineups are posted.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Josh Jung** (44.33). While he is a capable hitter, his matchup against Ryan is neutralized by a difficult SP skill profile, keeping him just behind the production floor set by our starters. **Miguel Vargas** (57.51) remains an intriguing case; while his base projection is modest, his score is bolstered significantly by a favorable wind forecast and a slow opposing delivery from Weathers that increases his stolen base potential\u2014an essential metric given our emphasis on speed. Conversely, **Wade Meckler** (40.91) barely clings to a starting role; he faces a challenging lefty-on-lefty matchup against Jump, and we will be monitoring the lineup card closely to ensure he isn't squeezed out of the order. While we remain thin with **Luis Robert Jr.** sidelined on the IL and **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** off today, we are banking on the high-contact approach of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (62.06) and the volume of our primary starters to maintain our efficiency targets.",
